-- arrived still spinning and the physics solver had to settle the assembly for several
-- frames after every jump -- that is the hitch you feel on each teleport. Zeroing the
-- angular velocity too means it lands dead-still, and skipping a move you are already
-- standing on avoids a pointless CFrame write (each write re-simulates the assembly).
