--  RESTRICTOR QUEST LINE  (Farm tab)
--    Sorcery Heavenly Restrictor  ->  SHR1 / SHR2 / SHR3  +  SHR4 exchange
--    Physical Heavenly Restrictor ->  PHR1 / PHR2 / PHR3  +  PHR4 + Invertion exchanges
--
--  Every id, level gate, prerequisite quest, point target and material list below is read LIVE
--  from ReplicatedStorage.Configs.QuestConfig -- none of it is typed in by hand, so it stays
--  correct if the game changes. Verified against the live game:
--    SHR1 Train I        Capture  Lv.100  1,000 pts  one-time
--    SHR2 Train II       Capture  Lv.150  1,500 pts  needs SHR1
--    SHR3 Train III      Capture  Lv.200  2,500 pts  needs SHR2
--    SHR4 Exchange       Lv.300   needs SHR3  5 AttackVow3 + 5 HeavenlyFragment + 1 SHRbinding -> SorceryHR
--    PHR1 Endurance I    Capture  Lv.100  1,000 pts  one-time
--    PHR2 Endurance II   Capture  Lv.150  1,500 pts  needs PHR1
--    PHR3 Endurance III  Capture  Lv.200  2,500 pts  needs PHR2
--    PHR4 Exchange       Lv.300   needs PHR3  5 AttackVow3 + 5 HeavenlyFragment + 1 PHRbinding -> PhysicalHR
--    Invertion Exchange  Lv.300   ONE-TIME    1 PhysicalHR + 1 InvertedFragment -> Invertion
--
--  All six quests are ordinary CAPTURE quests, exactly like Offense2 / StarCult2_1, so they are
--  driven by the SHARED Auto Quest pipeline (detect -> accept -> teleport -> bring -> farm ->
--  complete -> progress): NexoHRQuestId() feeds NexoRctQuestId() and NexoHRAnyOn() opens
--  NexoQuestEngineOn(). Nothing here re-implements farming -- this block only adds
--    * the accept / hand-in ladder (which claims the rewards)
--    * the prerequisite + level gates so the ladder can never get stuck on a locked quest
--    * the guarded exchanges (never fired without the materials, never fired twice)
--    * the two live requirement panels
--  ALL GLOBAL: the main chunk is near Luau's 200 local-register cap, so new locals here would
--  break the whole script.
--========================================================--
SHRQ1On, SHRQ2On, SHRQ3On = false, false, false
