-- What the summer raid gains from the swap (all previously missing here):
--   * cached join-pad resolution scoped inside QueueZones -- no full workspace walk, no lag spike,
--     and the raid MAP model can never be mistaken for the join part again
--   * real pad ANCHORING with drift correction + the actual countdown read off the pad nametag,
--     instead of blind fixed-frame teleport holds
--   * per-instance ISLAND LOCK -- it can only ever target NPCs inside the island YOU joined, so it
--     never steals or chases another player's summer island
--   * instant Retry on clear, plus an OUTSIDE-ISLAND watchdog and a STALL watchdog that restart the
--     whole flow from the queue step, so a broken run repairs itself
--   * a pcall SUPERVISOR around the entire flow -- an unexpected error can no longer kill the raid
--     thread permanently
--
-- Compatibility notes:
--   * Difficulty is pinned to 3 (Hard) because SummerSiege only offers Easy/Normal/Hard, unlike the
--     JJK raids that accept the Raid-tab Calamity default.
--   * All FIVE summer name-tags are passed as the boss tag list (multi-tag support added to
--     findNearestTaggedBoss), which reproduces exactly what collectSummerNPCs matched before.
--   * Both existing switches still work: "Auto Summer Raid" and the "Auto Raid" (FastRaidOn)
--     toggle each start the engine, and "Bring Summer Raid NPC" is untouched and still independent.
-- The helpers above (collectSummerNPCs / findSummerBoss / findSummerZone / summerGrabPos) are kept
-- because the Bring thread and the status readout still use them.
